[agent] **Done. The prediction distribution shifted on 2026-02-22**, and the answer `{"onset": "2026-02-22"}` is written to `submission/answers.json` and also persisted on the platform at `Resources/answers.json`.
[agent] How it ran (all analysis platform-side):
[agent] 1. **Ingestion** — created feature group `pred_log` v1 (ts as primary/event-time key, prediction as double), uploaded the CSV to HopsFS, and ran a platform Python job (`predlog_ingest`) that inserted all 13,380 rows and computed feature-group statistics. Direct client-side offline writes were impossible from this sandbox (raw-TCP HopsFS dials are blocked; only the HTTP proxy path works — I had to clear `NO_PROXY` since the default env excluded the cluster's 10.x subnet from the proxy), so cluster-side jobs did all data work.
[agent] 2. **Analysis** — a second platform job (`predlog_analyze`) read the feature group back through the Hopsworks Feature Query Service, computed per-day count/mean/std/median, and ran a two-segment least-squares change-point search over the daily means. (Trino SQL was attempted first but the offline table isn't Iceberg-format, so the iceberg catalog can't read it.)
[agent] The result is very clean: the daily mean sits at ~5.95 (std ~0.83) for every day from 2026-01-01 through 2026-02-21, then jumps to ~9.33 on 2026-02-22 and remains there through 2026-03-31 — a step change of about +3.4 (~4 standard deviations) with no gradual drift, so the onset date is unambiguous.
